{
"dur": 55.624,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 10.098,
"text": "Kentucky, 1973. A nine-year-old boy from Taiwan arrives at a boarding school in the hills, with his older brother. His parents have sold nearly everything to pay for it.",
"end": 10.373
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 10.373,
"vo_start": 10.648,
"vo_end": 17.552,
"text": "But it isn't the school they think it is. It's a reform school for troubled kids. His job there is cleaning the toilets, every day.",
"end": 17.827
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 17.827,
"vo_start": 18.102,
"vo_end": 25.697,
"text": "His roommate is seventeen, covered in tattoos and knife scars. Jensen teaches him to read. In return, the roommate teaches him to bench press.",
"end": 25.972
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 25.972,
"vo_start": 26.247,
"vo_end": 38.07,
"text": "In Oregon, from fifteen, he works nights at a Denny's: dishwasher, then busboy, then waiter. At Oregon State, his lab partner is a student named Lori Mills. They marry in 1985.",
"end": 38.345
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 38.345,
"vo_start": 38.62,
"vo_end": 49.52,
"text": "In 1993, in a booth at a Denny's in San Jose, he and two engineers start a company to make graphics chips. They put in two hundred dollars each. They call it Nvidia.",
"end": 49.795
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 49.795,
"vo_start": 50.07,
"vo_end": 54.674,
"text": "The first chip flops. By 1997 they have about a month of payroll left.",
"end": 55.624
}
],
